# ENV REGISTER: one verdict for every row of the engine's table this serve reads, and the value both env files write.
# The model (owner 2026-11-23): no row is left unset. scripts/env/prod.env and scripts/env/dev.env set every row of
# zig/src/platform/environment.zig whose scope is glm, cuda or common, at a measured value or at the engine's own default.
# Each line below is one row, in the table's order:
#   measured NAME=VALUE: a measurement chose it (its cells are in docs/KNOBS.md) or it was verified equal to the engine's
#     own computed answer; evidence names the record;
#   debt NAME=VALUE: set to the engine's own default and not measured on this stack; each is a lead, not permission.
# A row with no line is a hard stop (check-env-coverage.py), and a line whose value differs from the env files', whose row
# the table no longer has, or that uses the retired `default-ok` word fails the same gate.
#
# --- table rows of the applied tree: common, cuda, glm, one line each
# measured TF_CACHE_EVICT=main: queue98 E3 served decayed_resume: no gain, reply-equal; main stays; evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# inert TF_FLASHNEXT_BATCH_DRAWS=1: a Flash Next family row; this serve runs GLM; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# inert TF_STARTUP_RECEIPT=0: a receipt switch: it prints phases and changes no served path; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# inert TF_SHARED_PRICE_LOG=0: a log switch: no served path changes with it; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# inert TENSORFOLD_DEVICE_CHECK=1: a startup device check: its failure stops a boot, its success changes no timing; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# inert TENSORFOLD_VIDEO_TOKENS=16384: a vision path limit; this serve takes text; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# inert TENSORFOLD_MAX_PDF_PAGES=16: a PDF path limit; this serve takes text; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# launcher TENSORFOLD_PARALLEL=: : the row's default is no value (auto); serve.sh always passes --parallel, which wins; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# measured TENSORFOLD_PRESSURE_CACHE_PERCENT=50: queue129 screened 80 against 50 at 1, 2 and 4 clients: +0.27 -0.39 +0.67 percent, neutral; evidence docs/OVERNIGHT-2026-11-12.md
# measured TENSORFOLD_PREFIX_WAIT_MS=0: queue129 screened 200 against 0 at 1, 2 and 4 clients: +0.80 +1.10 +0.37 percent, positive at every level and under the 2 percent a screen needs, so the default stands as the undecided side; evidence docs/OVERNIGHT-2026-11-12.md
# inert TENSORFOLD_RESTORE_PREFETCH=2: the disk restore path's read-ahead; the tier's own arms are in docs/KNOBS.md; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# inert TENSORFOLD_RESTORE_PREFETCH_GIB=16: the disk restore path's budget; it prices disk, not a decode or prompt cell; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# inert TENSORFOLD_RESTORE_PREFETCH_MS=30000: the disk restore path's wait; it prices disk, not a decode or prompt cell; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# absent TENSORFOLD_TOOL_ID_KEY_FILE=: : no operator key file: the server makes a random key (the row's default); evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# absent TENSORFOLD_CUDA_KERNELS=: : no captured set: the engine discovers one beside the executable, else native; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# inert TF_NCCL_LIB=libnccl.so.2: plumbing: the library the ranks load, not a knob a boot can compare; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# inert TF_CUDA_DEVICE=0: the physical GPU ordinal; a Spark has one; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# inert TF_CUDA_SEGMENTS=1: an allocator shape; the pool and paging rows carry the behaviour a cell can move; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# inert TF_CUDA_CARVEOUT=0: the display-memory KV carveout is off on this serve; with it off this row decides nothing; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# inert TF_CUDA_CARVEOUT_MIB=1792: read only when the carveout is on, which it is not here; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# measured TF_MTP_DRAFTS=3: queue128 screened 1 against 3 at 1, 2 and 4 clients: -1.25 -1.29 +0.06 percent, neutral; evidence docs/OVERNIGHT-2026-11-12.md
# absent TF_DSPINE_WINDOW=: : the row's minimum is 16, so its reader's 0 (the drafter's own sliding_window) has no legal text; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# measured TF_DRAFT_NODES=15: screen with 8 at 1, 2 and 4 clients: +0.54 +1.12 +0.56 percent, UNCLEAR, the default stands; evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_QMMF_HALF_BELOW=96: queue128 screened 0 against 96 at 1, 2 and 4 clients: -1.18 -1.09 -0.31 percent, neutral; evidence docs/OVERNIGHT-2026-11-12.md
# inert TF_HY4_MEM_FLOOR_GIB=10: a Hy4-flash loader row; this serve loads GLM; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# launcher TENSORFOLD_MEMORY_RESERVE_GIB=: : serve.sh computes it per boot and per --parallel; the file states no value; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# absent TENSORFOLD_HIP_MEMORY_LIMIT_GB=: : no HIP limit: the row's default; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# inert TF_QWEN_KEEP_LATE=0: a Qwen family row; this serve runs GLM; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# absent TF_QWEN_KV_PAGE_TEST=: : the row's minimum is 1, so its reader's 0 (off) has no legal text; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# inert TF_COST_KEY_TRACE=0: a trace switch: no served path changes with it; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# inert TF_TIMING=0: timing prints: they cost time when on and change no cell when off; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# measured TF_NO_TREES=0: queue128 screened 1 against 0 at 1, 2 and 4 clients: -0.34 -0.96 +0.03 percent, neutral; evidence docs/OVERNIGHT-2026-11-12.md
# measured TF_MTP_TREES=0: queue129 screened 1 against 0 at 1, 2 and 4 clients: +0.97 +0.05 -0.82 percent, neutral; evidence docs/OVERNIGHT-2026-11-12.md
# measured TF_MTP_BATCH=1: queue129 screened 0 against 1 at 1, 2 and 4 clients: +0.51 +0.22 +0.23 percent, neutral; evidence docs/OVERNIGHT-2026-11-12.md
# inert TF_QWEN_POOL_LOG=0: a Qwen pool log; this serve runs GLM; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# absent TF_Q27_POCKET_OFF=: : no layer:neuron pairs: the row's default (off); evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# absent TF_Q27_TAIL=: : the row's only word is off; unset is each nudged sequence's tail rows, so no value; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# absent TF_Q27_GEMM=: : the row's only word is narrow; unset is 128x128 tiles; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# measured TENSORFOLD_PROMPT_CACHE_KEEP_OTHERS=0: queue132 screened 1 against 0 at 1, 2 and 4 clients: -0.69 -0.21 +0.01 percent, replies equal, neutral; evidence docs/OVERNIGHT-2026-11-12.md
# measured TF_PROMPT_INTERMEDIATE=0: queue132 screened 1 against 0 at 1, 2 and 4 clients: -0.31 -1.57 -0.22 percent, replies equal, neutral; evidence docs/OVERNIGHT-2026-11-12.md
# inert TENSORFOLD_LFM2_KV_PAGES=1: an LFM2 family row; this serve runs GLM; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# inert TENSORFOLD_UNIFIED_HOST_COUNTS=0: a counter switch: it reports, it does not compute; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# measured TF_ROCE_GID_INDEX=3: the search's own answer on all four HCAs of spark1 (RoCE v2 IPv4-mapped GID at index 3); evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# inert TF_QWEN35_CHUNK_SOLO=4096: a Qwen3.5 row; this serve runs GLM; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# measured TF_EXL3_DEC_ORDER=1: recipe: the routed-expert decode kernel set (OVERNIGHT section 24); evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# launcher TF_GLM_RANK=: : serve.sh passes the rank per boot; the file states no value; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# launcher TF_GLM_WORLD=: : serve.sh passes the world per boot; the file states no value; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# measured TF_GLM_HOST_CACHE=0: screen with 1 at 1, 2 and 4 clients: +2.42 -4.81 -1.70 percent, DEAD; evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# inert TF_GLM_VISION_HOST=0: the vision host path; this serve takes text; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# inert TF_GLM_PROF=0: the profiler: it is how a residual is read, and with it off it changes no cell; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# measured TF_GLM_LINK_WAIT=0: screen with 1 at 1, 2 and 4 clients: +1.26 +0.68 +1.41 percent, UNCLEAR; evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_PDL=1: queue91 mz1: PDL=0 is 2.48 to 4.02 percent lower over 12 cells; 1 is the default; evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_PROMPT_STEPS=1: screen with 0 at 1, 2 and 4 clients read PROMISING (+3.37 +2.36 +1.24), then the five-level arm made it a trade (-7.3 at six, +11.4 at eight): the default stands; evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_PROMPT_MANY=1: carried in both recipe sections since 2026-11-23; +1.55 / +5.45 / +2.96% at 1 / 4 / 8 clients on the mf1 image, two boots a group, replies identical (evidence docs/OVERNIGHT-2026-11-12.md section 114); the switch arrives with patches/port-multi-fill
# measured TF_GLM_SHARED=1: screen with 0 at 1, 2 and 4 clients: +2.52 -16.29 -34.34 percent, DEAD; evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_DSEL=1: screen with 0 at 1, 2 and 4 clients: -0.0 +0.4 -0.1 percent, neutral; evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_DSCORES=1: queue132 screened 0 against 1 at 1, 2 and 4 clients: -0.25 -0.55 +0.13 percent, replies equal, neutral; evidence docs/OVERNIGHT-2026-11-12.md
# inert TF_GLM_DFLASH2_LOG=0: a log switch: no served path changes with it; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# measured TF_GLM_DRAFT_CONFIDENCE=0.7: screen with 0.6 at 1, 2 and 4 clients: +1.12 +1.58 +0.85 percent, UNCLEAR; evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# absent TF_GLM_CONTEXT_CEILING=: : no ceiling: config.json's window stands (the row's default); evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# absent TF_GLM_EXPERT_FORM=: : no word: the load races classic against factored at each width (the row's default); evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# absent TF_GLM_KDA_DUMP=: : no dump file: the row's default; evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_DRAFT_ONEPASS=1: recipe: the drafter's one-pass linears; evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_DRAFT_DOWN4=1: recipe: the drafter MLP's down at 4 bits; evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_DRAFT_MLPSPLIT=4: recipe: split while at most four streams draft; evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_DRAFT_EDGE=0.6: recipe: the selector's edge weight (section 22); evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_DRAFT_BETA=2: recipe: the noisy-chance temperature (section 22); evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_DRAFT_NOISE=1: recipe: section 50; its 6 and 8 stream sampled cells are open; evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_DRAFT_CUTS=1:0.3: recipe: the chain cut by streams (section 22); evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_INDEX_DECODE_FROM=0: queue128 screened 8192 against 0 at 1, 2 and 4 clients: -0.03 +0.66 -0.31 percent, neutral; evidence docs/OVERNIGHT-2026-11-12.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_KEPT_WALK=1: recipe: the kept-state walk (OVERNIGHT section 17); evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_DECODE_INDEX=0: queue128 screened 1 against 0 at 1, 2 and 4 clients: +0.36 +0.27 -0.31 percent, neutral; evidence docs/OVERNIGHT-2026-11-12.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_NO_COPY=1: recipe: drafter windows without copied continuations (49); evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_ONEPASS_PIPE=1: recipe: the one-pass prompt pipe (49, 50); evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_MLA_FUSEMERGE=1: recipe: fused chunk and merge (section 17); evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_MULTI_FILL=0: measured -4.59 percent at four clients: not adopted; evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_ABSORB_VEC=1: recipe: promoted on the queue116 receipts (94, 95); evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_KVB8=0: queue132 screened 1 against 0 at 1, 2 and 4 clients: +4.23 +2.40 +2.28 percent, and the replies change at every level (four different digests) - a speed change may not alter replies, and upstream takes no mode that changes output tokens even opt-in, so it stays off; evidence docs/OVERNIGHT-2026-11-12.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_LATENT_ROWS=2: recipe: 2 rows a loop step (candidates, section 71); evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_SIDE_PRIO=1: recipe: promoted on the queue116 receipts (94, 95); evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_PIECE_FRONT=1: recipe: the front piece (section 58, candidates 71); evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_PIECE_FFN=1: recipe: the ffn site (section 58, candidates 71); evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_PIECE_MLA=1: recipe: the MLA site (section 58, candidates 71); evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_SOLO_TO_START=1: recipe: sections 64, 68; row owned by solo-cuts/0001; evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_RESTORE_HELD=1: recipe: sections 65, 69 (queue90); evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_FRONT_ROWS=0: 512, 768 and 2048 measured: 2048 slower on warm turns (3.2 to 3.8) and on the cold prompt, 512 and 768 no gain: the default stands; evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_MM_WIDE=1: recipe: 32 x 32 warp prompt blocks (94, 95); evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_MM_DECTILE=100000: recipe: 16-row decode tiles (49, 50); evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_SWIGLU_REDUCE=1: recipe: reduce and SwiGLU in one launch (49, 50); evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_GLUE_FUSE=0: measured neutral: -2 percent in the first cells and -0.6 to +1.4 repeated; evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_GLUE_ROW=0: cold prompts at 8k and 32k within 1.4 percent of the control, which itself differs by 2 percent: no gain; evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_PDL_EARLY=0: two sets of cells, -0.6 -0.9 0.0 -0.1 +0.5 and a repeat of -0.4 -0.4 -0.3 -0.1 +0.3: neutral; evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_HOST_ONCE=1: recipe: a request rendered once (49); fresh 6/8 cells open; evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_OFF_EFFORT_LINE=1: recipe: production's prompt, no speed cell (section 45); evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_X3_NC=1: recipe: the routed-expert decode trellis (24); evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_X3_XROW=1: recipe: the xrow load (24); evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_X3_FUSEDOWN=1: recipe: the fused down (24); evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_KEEP_SEQS=1: recipe: sections 30 and 34; evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# measured TF_GLM_OVN_DISK_SLICE_MIB=0: queue132 screened 16 against 0 at 1, 2 and 4 clients: -0.80 -0.19 +0.16 percent, replies equal, neutral; evidence docs/OVERNIGHT-2026-11-12.md
# measured TF_GLM_INDEX_CUDA=1: with the X3_NC, DECODE_INDEX and DRAFT_CUTS arms on the final recipe over ten cells: mean -0.55 percent, neutral; evidence docs/KNOBS.md
# absent TF_GLM_KV_HOST_GIB=: : no amount named: one full window and 16 rows a page (the default); evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
#
# --- set in the env files with no row of the table (read through a raw getenv; check-env.py rule 5)
# A table row is the ideal for each of these six: the register can then judge its value, not only its reader.
# raw TF_GLM_CHUNK_SOLO=4096: a solo prompt pass's rows; read through a raw getenv, a table row is the ideal (zig/src/families/glm/cuda_ranks.zig); evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# raw TF_GLM_DENSE_BITS=4: the dense linears' packing; read through a raw getenv, a table row is the ideal (zig/src/families/glm/cuda_ranks.zig); evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# raw TF_GLM_HEAD_BITS=8: the head's packing; read through a raw getenv, a table row is the ideal (zig/src/families/glm/cuda_ranks.zig); evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# raw TF_GLM_KDA_PAD=1: the KDA input stack padded to the common width; raw getenv, a table row is the ideal (zig/src/families/glm/cuda_kda_block.zig); evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# raw TF_GLM_OVERLAP_PIECES=4: a prompt chunk's exchanges in row pieces; raw getenv, a table row is the ideal (zig/src/families/glm/cuda_ranks.zig); evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
# raw TENSORFOLD_NO_UPDATE_CHECK=1: the update check off; raw getenv, a table row is the ideal (zig/src/server/benchmark_server.zig); evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md
#
# --- dev.env's candidates: the measured value a KNOBS=dev boot runs over prod's default
#
# --- set by the launcher, never a line of the env files
# launcher TF_GLM_RANK: serve.sh passes the rank per boot (the env file's line is blank so the boot always wins)
# launcher TF_GLM_WORLD: serve.sh passes the world per boot (the env file's line is blank)
# launcher TENSORFOLD_MEMORY_RESERVE_GIB: serve.sh computes it from --parallel per boot (the env file's line is blank)
# launcher TF_GLM_ROCE_MULTI: serve.sh adds it at world above 1 and --parallel at most 4 when the mailbox image exists
# launcher TF_TP_MASTER: serve.sh adds it with TF_GLM_ROCE_MULTI
# launcher TF_TP_KERNEL_IMAGE: serve.sh adds it with TF_GLM_ROCE_MULTI
# launcher NCCL_COMM_ID: computed by the launching chain; serve.sh requires it above one rank
# --- external, read by NCCL and the Hugging Face client, not by the engine's table: NCCL_*, HF_HUB_OFFLINE.
